the invisible election isn't just about  political parties activities or what  unknown third parties get up to as well  Sky News has uncovered the existence of  previously unknown botnets networks of  automated social media accounts  spreading political messages  and we've tracked how they've been  influencing the election through  thousands of tweets the botnets that  we've picked up were tweeting the same  thing at the same time that's very  stupid bots which tweet hundreds of  thousands of times per day are also very  stupid are very easy to pick up they can  be very effective at shutting down  debate we collaborated with the center  of the analysis of social media to look  into BOTS  during this election if you're trying to  be a real person and pretend that you're  real person you need to employ some  quite sophisticated tactics to get  people to believe that you are indeed  just concerned about Jeremy Corbyn or  politics in Britain according to the  research the bots in this election have  been small-scale and subtle hard to tell  from humans that compares with a much  larger scale sledgehammer approach in  other campaigns in 2014 in Mexico the  government used around 75,000 BOTS to  tweet spam material and drown out  protests in Russia after the  assassination of opposition politician  Boris Nemtsov BOTS were used to spread  misinformation about who is behind the  killing and all around the world BOTS  have been used by politicians to make  them seem much more popular than they  actually are  we call it computational propaganda it's  the combination of a computer program  that gets a message out to thousands of  thousands of users with some piece of  junk news or some some fake facts that  have been made up that try to poison  conversations the problem with BOTS  isn't necessarily someone with a lot of  computing power cranking their servers  to swing an election it's  the uncertainty they so you might think  that you're speaking to an authentic  unique online voice but perhaps you're  chatting to automated software in stay  in undermines the credibility of  everyone when you can't answer the  simple question BOTS or not throughout  this campaign we've tried to uncover the  hidden digital techniques of modern  political persuasion the pause will be  the visible result of this most  invisible election Tom Cheshire Sky News
 

